The Fundamental Concept Audit #21, on the shape audit #20 had no scope
for: two consumers computing ONE fact independently and disagreeing.
Every earlier instance (WI-jufih, WI-zulij, INV-hokig, INV-pazur,
WI-punod, WI-bobuf) was found by its symptom and fixed alone.

Method: four read-only sub-agents, one per family (reachability,
ranking and scope, counts and pass disclosure, classification and
tier), AST walks for every derivation on the pinned tree a17367f254;
each separate pair measured on one default survey per language family
(mitmproxy, knex, logrus, ripgrep, jedis), every counted disagreement
read against source, the highest-impact code claims re-checked.

Confirmed: of 17 facts, 12 are derived separately. On real output:
- five test predicates; ripgrep's #[test] functions in src/ are 434 of
  dead-code's 817 candidates and 493 of test-coverage's 2,680
  production functions, while slice and io-boundaries call them tests;
- dead-code and test-coverage walk different edge sets: 12 overrides
  reached by dispatches_to are test-only to one and untested to the
  other (mitmproxy, knex, ripgrep 4 each);
- io-boundaries and taint disagree on 18 of 1,488 edges: taint ignores
  io_target_kind (a redirect to /dev/null, Fprintf into a buffer) and
  reads process.on lifecycle handlers as untrusted input.
14 items filed, each named beside its verdict in the document.

WI-vosop, decided by the sweep: the harness and a live survey of the
recorded aardvark-dns crate differed on calls/in-repo (93/19/7 vs
92/17/8). Edge by edge: the survey dedups with remove_self_loops=True
and the harness did not (3 false self-bindings); a survey's sorted file
order makes the Rust analyzer bind serve.rs:287 to a #[cfg(test)]
helper (a defect, WI-lirik); the survey's file nodes add every imports
edge and 11 module-level calls.
- _two_arm_artifact dedups with the survey's flag: 93/16/7.
- 0019's Reading states what its edge rows describe.
- Its guard checked only the header and attribute rows, and the table
  kept a 269 references row and a pre-WI-bamar type_alias row; it now
  checks every pairing and edge row against the instrument (mutation-
  checked: the old table reds on type_alias, a 269 edge row on
